# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  RAG-Based AI Document Analyser — Environment Configuration
#
#  HOW TO USE:
#    1. Copy this file:  Copy-Item .env.example .env
#    2. Edit .env with your settings
#    3. The application works with ALL values commented out —
#       it falls back to extractive (no-LLM) mode automatically.
#
#  SECURITY:
#    - Never commit .env to version control
#    - .env is listed in .gitignore
#    - API keys are loaded from this file only, never hardcoded
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Option A: Local GGUF model (llama-cpp-python) ──────────────────
#
# Download a GGUF model, e.g.:
#   Mistral-7B Q4_K_M (~4 GB, good quality/speed balance):
#   https://huggingface.co/TheBloke/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2-GGUF
#
# Install Python binding:
#   pip install llama-cpp-python
#
# Then uncomment and set the path below (use forward slashes):
#
# GGUF_MODEL_PATH=C:/models/mistral-7b-instruct-v0.2.Q4_K_M.gguf


# ── Option B: OpenAI-compatible API ────────────────────────────────
#
# Works with: OpenAI, Groq, Together AI, Ollama, Anyscale, etc.
#
# OpenAI:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL_NAME=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Groq (free tier available):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=gsk_...
# OPENAI_API_BASE=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL_NAME=llama3-8b-8192
#
# Ollama (local server, free):
# OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama
# OPENAI_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL_NAME=mistral


# ── Embeddings (optional override) ────────────────────────────────
#
# Default: sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
#   - 384 dimensions, ~22 MB, fast on CPU
#
# Higher quality (slower, 768 dims, ~420 MB):
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2
#
# IMPORTANT: If you change this, you must re-process all documents.
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2


# ── FAISS index persistence (optional) ────────────────────────────
#
# If set, the vector index is saved to disk so documents do not
# need to be re-processed on every application restart.
# The directory is created automatically.
#
# FAISS_INDEX_DIR=./faiss_store
